# Fibonacci Function

Here's a JavaScript function that generates the first n Fibonacci numbers:

```javascript
function fibonacci(n) {
  // Handle edge cases
  if (n <= 0) {
    return [];
  }

  if (n === 1) {
    return [0];
  }

  if (n === 2) {
    return [0, 1];
  }

  // Initialize array with first two Fibonacci numbers
  const result = [0, 1];

  // Generate remaining Fibonacci numbers
  for (let i = 2; i < n; i++) {
    result.push(result[i - 1] + result[i - 2]);
  }

  return result;
}
```

